//@version=6
indicator("UCTPROBE_VW_W4_T15_LOOP_TAIL_VALUE", overlay = false)

// PROVENANCE: written 2026-11-07 for the Pine parity programme, capture queue row W4-T15-b
// (docs/pine/capture-queue-2026-11-05-w4-t15-t17.md). NEVER COMPILED ON TRADINGVIEW.
// The VALUE of a loop (a function's last statement) whose body ENDS in something other than a plain
// value line; the runtime lane keeps these valueless. Each loop runs i = 0..3:
//   F01  body ends in an `if` / `else` chain    (i odd -> i, even -> -i): last pass -> 3 ?
//   F02  body ends in a call, math.max(i, 2)    last pass -> 3 ?
//   F03  body ends in a tuple [i, i * 2]        read as [P, Q]: last pass -> 3, 6 ?
// Every bar carries the same values; one bar settles it. If a row does not compile, the error
// names its line: split that row out and capture the rest (the tuple tail is the likeliest).
// CHART: the row names none (the queue marks it NEEDS_CHART). Inputs at defaults.

fIfTail() =>
    for i = 0 to 3
        if i % 2 == 1
            i
        else
            0 - i

fCallTail() =>
    for i = 0 to 3
        math.max(i, 2)

fTupleTail() =>
    for i = 0 to 3
        [i, i * 2]

[p, q] = fTupleTail()

plot(bar_index, "A00_bar_index_CONTROL")
plot(fIfTail(), "F01_if_chain_tail_value")
plot(fCallTail(), "F02_call_tail_value")
plot(p, "F03a_tuple_tail_first")
plot(q, "F03b_tuple_tail_second")
